unBudget: its usage is not in recordUsage, run cost or the subject/tenant/fleet quotas. measureBeforeCall (context-size.ts:35 countTokens) is also unmetered. The main call (loop.ts:61) is charged only after it returns (recordUsage at loop.ts:63), and the SDK client retries once (loop.ts:15 maxRetries: 1) uncounted.\"\nA check B07.4 --met no --evidence src/agent/classifier.ts:45 --quote 'res = await client.messages.create(' --note \"Classifier calls run for every inbound message before any budget exists in the call path, so the per-subject/tenant/fleet daily cost quotas do not count them. Main-call quotas are charged after the call (budget.ts:139-141), with no finite bound on concurrent runs.\"\n# B08\nA check B08.2 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:63 --quote 'const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \"string\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;' --note \"clinicId comes from model tool input, not from ctx.tenantId alone, and no check ties it to the caller's tenant or to a sibling group. It selects per-clinic secrets, EHR session and payment/SMS keys. The runtime IAM role reads all clinic-agent/* secrets (iam.tf:35), so one pod holds credentials for every tenant.\"\nA check B08.3 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:63 --quote 'const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \"string\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;' --note \"Tenant separation is decided by a value the model emits; no infrastructure rule (per-tenant role or namespace) sits behind it. The NetworkPolicy (deployment.yaml:162) is infrastructure but does not separate tenants.\"\n# B09\nA check B09.1 --met unknown --evidence k8s/deployment.yaml:189 --quote 'matchLabels: { app: egress-proxy }' --note \"NetworkPolicy allows egress only to DNS, the platform egress proxy and a /28. The destination allowlist lives in the proxy (platform namespace), described only in the comment at deployment.yaml:160; its rules are outside this repo.\"\nA check B09.2 --met unknown -