{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDUxuM21T1WcMLkv1sDB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B06–B10, and all five items are rated `gap`. The batch validation passes (`--batch B06,B07,B08,B09,B10 --before-challenges --fix`, \"Valid. gap: 5\"). The findings are saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`. I did not run challenges, run the repo, or add other items.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| B06 Approval integrity (G1) | gap, high confidence | `checkApproval` (`src/tools/approvals.ts:60-82`) never compares the stored `argsHash` or `agentInstanceId`. Approvals are never marked used, so one approval id can be replayed with different arguments until it expires. No permission or resource-state recheck runs before the tool does. A store error does deny (B06.5 is a yes). B06.1 is unknown because `hashArgs` drops nested argument content and the `cancel_appointment` schema isn't in the repo. |\n| B07 Hard execution budgets (G2) | gap, high | The classifier model call (`src/agent/classifier.ts:45`) and the `countTokens` call (`src/agent/context-size.ts:35`) are not counted in any budget or quota. The main call is charged only after it returns, and the SDK retry (`maxRetries: 1`) is uncounted. The six limits are set and no sub-agents are started (B07.1 and B07.3 are yes). |\n| B08 Environment isolation (G2) | gap, high | The model chooses `clinicId` (`src/tools/executor.ts:63`) with no check against the caller's tenant. The runtime IAM role reads every clinic's secrets (`infra/terraform/iam.tf:35`). The NetworkPolicy is default-deny with named peers (B08.1 is a yes). |\n| B09 Egress allowlist (G2) | gap, medium | `createRemoteJWKSet(new URL(header.jku))` in `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:83` fetches a URL from an unverified header, and no fetch in the repo checks redirects or resolved IPs. The proxy allowlist, IPv6 handling, per-resource limits and block alerting are outside the repo (B09.1, B09.2, B09.4 and B09.5 are unknown). Only the external proxy could block those fetches. |\n| B10 Pinned, verified image (G2) | gap, medium | Provenance is generated in `ci.yml` but never verified. The deploy check at `deploy.yml:69` is `grep -q \"$DIGEST\" k8s/deployment.yaml`. That passes if the digest appears anywhere in the file, including the `IMAGE_DIGEST` env values, so an `image:` line with a different digest could slip through. There is no admission policy in the repo (B10.2 and B10.4 are unknown). Images are pinned by digest and Cosign is v2.6.2 (B10.1 and B10.5 are yes). |\n\n- **Prescan:** it had 11 hits, all for other items (B02, B11, R13, E03). I left them unresolved for those items' batches and noted that in `scope`. I found no injection attempts in the repo.\n- **Interpreter slip:** early on I ran one read-only JSON summary with `python3` instead of your required interpreter. It only parsed `batch-policy.json`; everything after that used the specified one.\n- **Edits outside `answer.py`:** I set the `scope` text and removed a mistaken self-reference in B08's `also_affects` by editing the findings file directly, since `answer.py` doesn't cover those.\n- **Scratch files:** the coverage JSON files are in `work/`, and the prescan and inventory output is in `agent/` (`brace-prescan.json`, `brace-inventory.json`)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":728,"cache_read_input_tokens":94738,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":728},"output_tokens":808,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c726312-2a50-4db8-a6b3-1ad588dc6531","uuid":"b186afc9-2110-412e-b4b6-03a8c9e570b6","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:23:54.308Z","request_id":"req_011CgDUxu1vRHifo78H8BQPb"}
